      {
        "id": 227670,
        "name": "rjc917",
        "username": "rjc917",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rjc917/{size}/1888_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-05-28T13:01:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Allowing yourself or another spirit to place extra presence would probably count as utility too.&nbsp; And I actually wonder if removing blight wouldn't count as utility rather than defense.&nbsp; Cleaning up the mess that was already made isn't really defending to me.</p>\n<p>Now I'm wondering how it was determined exactly how big each of those stat bars should be.&nbsp; Obviously they can be generally figured out e.g.&nbsp;this spirit is really good at defense, but doesn't produce much fear so fear should be low and defense should be high, but is there some formula for exactly how big to make them?</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:01:55.129Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 6,
        "reads": 3,
        "readers_count": 2,
        "score": 30.6,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19211,
        "topic_slug": "what-do-control-utility-really-mean",
        "display_username": "rjc917",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Allowing yourself or another spirit to place extra presence would probably count as utility too.&nbsp; And I actually wonder if removing blight wouldn't count as utility rather than defense.&nbsp; Cleaning up the mess that was already made isn't really defending to me.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Now I'm wondering how it was determined exactly how big each of those stat bars should be.&nbsp; Obviously they can be generally figured out e.g.&nbsp;this spirit is really good at defense, but doesn't produce much fear so fear should be low and defense should be high, but is there some formula for exactly how big to make them?</p>",
